Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zero-setup model access: after sign-in the renderer hands its metering-proxy
device key to main (nemesis:llm:sync IPC), which writes DEEPSEEK_API_KEY +
DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL into $HERMES_HOME/.env (upsertEnvVars, tested) and restarts
local backends — chat works on a fresh install with no provider setup. The
upstream provider onboarding overlay is suppressed in the student build.

Desktop Google/Apple sign-in: account gate buttons open the browser at
app.enternemesis.com/auth/desktop with a one-shot state nonce; the session
returns through the nemesis://auth deep link (refresh token only, exchanged
with Supabase before trust; state checked). Sign-out now drops the device key
so a second student on the same Mac mints their own.

Account & usage settings: the Usage page (restored for students) gains account
status (email/plan/trial/renewal, manage/refresh/sign out) and a 7-day usage
bar chart read from the student's own RLS-scoped counters. Settings also gains
a Keyboard shortcuts entry that opens the existing keybind panel.

Student empty start: Study no longer seeds demo pharm decks. Persona is field-
neutral (any major) in SOUL/prompt-builder/recorder prompts; old app-written
SOULs auto-upgrade. Consent copy: partner categories on screen, named list in
the linked Privacy Policy. Projects view toggle un-hidden for students (create
a project mid-session). NSLocalNetworkUsageDescription added.
